-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of S/tS when Ω_{S/A} is free on dt
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $S$ a commutative $A$-algebra which is formally smooth over $A$, and let $t \in S$ be an element with the property that every element $\omega$ of the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{S/A}$ admits a unique $s \in S$ with $\omega = s \cdot D_{A/S}(t)$, i.e. $\Omega_{S/A}$ is free of rank one on the basis $dt$ (existence and uniqueness of the coefficient are both part of the hypothesis). The conclusion is that the quotient $S / (t)$, where $(t)$ is the ideal of $S$ generated by the single element $t$, is again formally smooth as an $A$-algebra, the $A$-algebra structure being the one induced from $S$. Here formal smoothness is the infinitesimal lifting property in Mathlib's sense: every $A$-algebra map from the ring in question to a quotient $B/I$ by a square-zero ideal lifts to an $A$-algebra map to $B$.
--
--   This is the statement that the zero fibre of an étale coordinate is formally smooth over the base: if $t$ cuts out a relative divisor along which $dt$ trivialises $\Omega_{S/A}$, then $A \to S/tS$ is formally smooth. It is used in the construction of sections of a smooth curve through a point of order one in the local ring, via [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus).
